---
const stages = [
  ['baseline', 'the code as shipped', '3', '188', '50', '81'],
  ['0001', 'duplication and constants', '3', '190', '40', '60'],
  ['0002', 'function shapes', '3', '210', '20', '37'],
  ['0003', 'structure', '13', '449', '4', '4'],
];
---

<section id="demo" class="border-b-2 border-base-300">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-16 lg:py-20">
    <div class="max-w-2xl space-y-3">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.2em] text-primary uppercase">One command</p>
      <h2 class="font-display text-4xl sm:text-5xl">Point it at code and watch it work</h2>
      <p class="text-base-content/70">
        <code class="font-mono text-sm">demo/</code> is a small Model Context Protocol server, written
        badly on purpose, that ships in the repository so a fresh checkout has something real to
        check. <code class="font-mono text-sm">demo/stages/</code> holds the three patches that take
        it from fifty failures to four.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:items-start">
      <div class="border-2 border-base-content bg-neutral text-neutral-content overflow-x-auto">
        <div class="border-base-300/30 flex items-center gap-2 border-b-2 px-4 py-2">
          <span class="bg-primary size-2.5 rounded-full"></span>
          <span class="bg-secondary size-2.5 rounded-full"></span>
          <span class="size-2.5 rounded-full bg-neutral-content/40"></span>
          <span class="text-neutral-content/50 ml-2 font-mono text-xs">demo/ · terminal</span>
        </div>
        <pre class="p-5 font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed sm:text-sm"><code>{`$ mcmr check demo/ --no-contextual

3 files, 188 facts, 194/211 rules, 17 skipped,
194 table queries, 2313 observations,
50 failures, 81 findings, 0 unassessed,
kernel 140 ms, rules 525 ms`}</code></pre>
      </div>

      <div class="overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="table-zebra table border-2 border-base-content text-sm">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th class="font-mono text-xs font-normal opacity-60">stage</th>
              <th class="font-mono text-xs font-normal opacity-60">theme</th>
              <th class="font-mono text-xs font-normal opacity-60">files</th>
              <th class="font-mono text-xs font-normal opacity-60">facts</th>
              <th class="font-mono text-xs font-normal opacity-60">failures</th>
              <th class="font-mono text-xs font-normal opacity-60">findings</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {
              stages.map(([stage, theme, files, facts, failures, findings]) => (
                <tr>
                  <th class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold">{stage}</th>
                  <td class="opacity-80">{theme}</td>
                  <td class="opacity-70">{files}</td>
                  <td class="opacity-70">{facts}</td>
                  <td class="text-primary font-bold">{failures}</td>
                  <td class="opacity-70">{findings}</td>
                </tr>
              ))
            }
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p class="text-base-content/60 mt-4 text-sm">
          Every stage keeps <code class="font-mono text-xs">python demo/smoke.py</code> passing. Four
          findings survive on purpose, an unbuilt protocol surface, a deliberate dependency trade,
          and two settings for a test suite this directory does not have yet.
        </p>
        <a href="/mcmr/docs/start/demo-walkthrough/" class="btn btn-primary btn-sm mt-4">
          Walk through all three stages
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
